Use `ConfigureLifecycleEvents` in `MauiProgram.cs` to hook directly into native callbacks:

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
#if ANDROID
    events.AddAndroid(android => android
        .OnPause(activity => {
            // App losing focus / partially hidden
        })
        .OnStop(activity => {
            // App fully backgrounded
        }));
#elif IOS || MACCATALYST
    events.AddiOS(ios => ios
        .DidEnterBackground(app => {
            // App entered background
        }));
#endif
});
```

**Alternatively**, if you don't need the native objects (e.g., `activity`, `app`), use the cross-platform `Window.Stopped` event which maps to both Android `OnStop` and iOS `DidEnterBackground`:

```csharp
// In App.cs
protected override Window CreateWindow(IActivationState? activationState)
{
    var window = base.CreateWindow(activationState);
    window.Stopped += (s, e) => { /* runs on background for all platforms */ };
    return window;
}
```

**Key notes:**
- `OnPause` (Android) = `Deactivated` (loss of focus, not necessarily backgrounded)
- `OnStop` (Android) / `DidEnterBackground` (iOS) = `Stopped` (fully backgrounded)
- Keep handlers fast (<2s) to avoid ANR/watchdog kills
- On Android, also handle `Destroying` — the back button can skip `Stopped` entirely
